{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787354433078060001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"catchable-clueless-rhino","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f336e6be218ee86bbc30a10ab6f492fe6aa626d39b869a8adfb550bd3d8904a1","event_uuid":"c52a397e-3c04-4e3c-af27-080fd335c846","position":{"commit_sha":"8c991d8cb713e521c6ed8783f44872f151f2a8e3","position":"1787352383291423001-c52a397e-3c04-4e3c-af27-080fd335c846"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f5df785f7ba767a79bff4a5728df26d7647eb2f40f16517268841752d748345b","event_uuid":"8e14d6d9-2859-4018-9cc1-ab5af71b2d95","position":{"commit_sha":"08e529100d686ce279878fb52c2d0a07707bb50a","position":"1787352388984328001-8e14d6d9-2859-4018-9cc1-ab5af71b2d95"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787352383291423001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nLLM failure classification is duplicated: the context-length heuristic is byte-identical in `src/rebar/llm/failure.py:152` and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:316-329` (comment at `failure.py:146` says \"stay in sync\"); the stop-reason→message map exists in `src/rebar/llm/structured.py:622,632` and `failure.py:355`; the retryable→exit-code mapping is hand-composed in four CLI verbs (`src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:46-98,162,236-247,341`), `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:27-34,239`, and `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:656-686`. Bug `injurious-definable-badger` (content-filter denial reported as \"too large\") hid exactly at the seam where one caller composed `message_for(...)` without the `finish_reason`.\n\n## Approach\nMake `failure.py` the only classifier: `sizing.py` imports `_CONTEXT_LEN_HINTS`; `structured.py` derives its messages from `message_for`; add `failure.exit_code_for(outcome_or_coverage) -> int` and `failure.mcp_payload_for(...)` used by the four verbs, MCP, and `close_precheck`. Guard: the context-length hint strings and the `content_filter` message literal appear only in `failure.py`.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/failure.py`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py`, `src/rebar/llm/structured.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, `tests/unit/llm/test_failure_exit_codes.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nTable test: every (exception, finish_reason) pair in the existing fixtures yields the same class, message, exit code, and MCP payload as today across all six callers. Edge: `content_filter` with and without `finish_reason` yields the content-filter message on every caller. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_llm_failure*.py`, `tests/unit/test_close_gate_bound_remedy_db1c.py`, `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_recovery_contract.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"maximum context length\" src/rebar` returns one file; checked by the grep and the guard test.\n- [ ] Exit codes 11/1/2 for every fixture outcome are identical across the six callers; checked by the table test.\n- [ ] Pinning suites pass unchanged; checked by `pytest`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/failure.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"tests/unit/llm/test_failure_exit_codes.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"fcb7-e6e2-7244-42d2","ticket_type":"story","title":"failure.py as the sole LLM failure classifier with shared exit-code mapping","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c52a397e-3c04-4e3c-af27-080fd335c846","8e14d6d9-2859-4018-9cc1-ab5af71b2d95"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787354433078060001,"uuid":"40f94d06-6f00-4f43-9328-32c01dfc382a"}